Misty page: icons, open-the-box reveal, the maths with totals, plain-words narration, proof folded

- placeholder icons on every outcome (picked from words in the label) on
  the spin strip, the result, the box tiles and all tables
- reveal switch: Open the box (shared box-opening animation, default) or
  Misty's spin strip
- "The maths of this box": worth x chance = cost per open for every row,
  subtotals for Mistees and pieces, the total, the box price and what the
  operator keeps, on screen and really; the same totals under the
  back-office odds editor
- narration rewritten in plain words (no hash, fingerprint or HMAC): how
  often the result happens, what it is worth on screen and really, the net
  of the open in real money, the bands on the 0 to 100 line with the roll
  marked
- proof panel: plain what-this-proves summary, technical rows behind a
  button; the recipe in settings moved under "for developers"

